"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:48:13-08:00","id":832931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=832929#post832929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... and now to make a random generator for kith + seeming mixes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gosh. That could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:55:11-08:00","id":832938,"title":"","content":"Hooray for the Swimmerskin.<br /> <br /> What might Needle and Thread be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:55:51-08:00","id":832939,"title":"","content":"Actually, something just struck me: There really isn't a &quot;concubine&quot; kith. I think the closest thing is Deerheart, but that seems more like a confidante than &quot;bed warmer&quot; (though the Darkling version does mention incubi/succubi, the mechanics are more about disarming than seducing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:05:57-08:00","id":832943,"title":"","content":"Mr. Hill you really are spoiling all of us. Is this a plot to lure us to Arcadia? Because if it is, it's working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:10:02-08:00","id":832945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=832939#post832939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, something just struck me: There really isn't a &quot;concubine&quot; kith. I think the closest thing is Deerheart, but that seems more like a confidante than &quot;bed warmer&quot; (though the Darkling version does mention incubi/succubi, the mechanics are more about disarming than seducing).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a place I was a bit uncomfortable and not in a good way. So while I don't preclude those types of characters from occurring, I didn't want to spell them out so explicitly. I found that not being so explicit meant players tended to favor nuance when they played those types of characters, so it was a win-win situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:16:58-08:00","id":832950,"title":"","content":"Fair enough! I can't disagree with any of that in the slightest, and I definitely approve of the idea behind it. I admit that angle hadn't really occurred to me when I wrote my previous post.<br /> <br /> Originally I was thinking that mechanically, it's hard to find a &quot;neutral&quot; Blessing for a seduction-focused changeling (Flamesiren is fire-themed, Nix is water-themed, others are music-themed, and so on). That said, I think Deerheart does the job well enough, since I'm sure there can be specific Contracts made to make the changeling more physically appealing or better at seduction, and the Deerheart's Blessing synergises well with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:47:00-08:00","id":832961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=832929#post832929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... and now to make a random generator for kith + seeming mixes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need this! Whole customization possibilities are, literally, made me stuck at a standstill on creating character concept for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/831923-changeling-playtest-game\">Forum Playtests</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's just too much to choose from without clear character concept... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some limitation on 10 random ideas would be GOD SEND, just to limit creative pool a bit.<br /> <br /> ( No, I <b>do not</b> complain about the number of combinations available when creating a character in 2ED - I'm just saying that the generator is a REALLY good idea for people like me, to limit all combinations a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Will read now new Kiths, maybe something really cool will speak from them to me and I will have my character concept, finally. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:33:13-08:00","id":832986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>machineIV</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Oh gosh. That could be fun.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=832961#post832961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really need this! Whole customization possibilities are, literally, made me stuck at a standstill on creating character concept for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/831923-changeling-playtest-game\">Forum Playtests</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's just too much to choose from without clear character concept... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some limitation on 10 random ideas would be GOD SEND, just to limit creative pool a bit.<br /> <br /> ( No, I <b>do not</b> complain about the number of combinations available when creating a character in 2ED - I'm just saying that the generator is a REALLY good idea for people like me, to limit all combinations a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.... For some reason the commands to make it executable by other people isn't working for me. I'll try to figureout a way to get my computer to actually work. In the mean time, anyone who knows java can use <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/7k3hwWR1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. It generates six changelings + 1 changeling with dual-kith. Once I get more freetime I might put an actual interface rather than using commands, so it's not painful to use. But this is just a quick-thing right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-18-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:05:55-08:00","id":833002,"title":"","content":"This is cool.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I don't love the corpesgrinder blessing because I do, but out of curiousity, would you entertain adding a kind of benefit to reflect the flavor of them eating corpses?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what to do with it, since stuff like regaining health from eating corpses is rather macabre, but it strikes me that while their benefit is cool for killing stuff, it'd be nice if they had a component to do with their function too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:13:42-08:00","id":833004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833002#post833002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying I don't love the corpesgrinder blessing because I do, but out of curiousity, would you entertain adding a kind of benefit to reflect the flavor of them eating corpses?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what to do with it, since stuff like regaining health from eating corpses is rather macabre, but it strikes me that while their benefit is cool for killing stuff, it'd be nice if they had a component to do with their function too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can concur, as I was just thinking about Arabian Ghul character based on Corpesgrinder I got some thought on Kith's Blessing:<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Blow others is cool power, but &quot;losing Defense&quot; part on victim is very restrictive in gameplay use</b> - I understand why it's limited by this, but then whole Blessing sounds a much weaker, compared to other Kiths ( Flamesiren at least ). Maybe adding some nice small additional benefit to be used on day-to-day activity? <b>Like maybe healing by eating human flesh?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:26:04-08:00","id":833010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833004#post833004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can concur, as I was just thinking about Arabian Ghul character based on Corpesgrinder I got some thought on Kith's Blessing:<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Blow others is cool power, but &quot;losing Defense&quot; part on victim is very restrictive in gameplay use</b> - I understand why it's limited by this, but then whole Blessing sounds a much weaker, compared to other Kiths ( Flamesiren at least ). Maybe adding some nice small additional benefit to be used on day-to-day activity? <b>Like maybe healing by eating human flesh?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Killing Blow is weak at all. If somebody's got the Bleeding Tilts for example and you Surprise them, they're in for trouble. Or if they're undead, just surprise them.<br /> <br /> Also consider: They All-out Attack, or you use one of the merits that denies people their defense for a turn, or they've been attacked by enough people to wear it down.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of circumstance where it might apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:30:00-08:00","id":833011,"title":"","content":"Ugh, I thought the Dearheart kith was called DEERheart because of... something something doe eyes?<br /> <br /> There are not enough facepalms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:34:09-08:00","id":833014,"title":"","content":"Take the Dual Kith Merit and mixed a Darkling Dearheart/Flamesiren for a demonic Succubus. He/She can see in darkness, has the sympathetic merit (what ever that is), can give someone the swoon condition, is fiery to that person's touch, gets \u2022\u2022 Striking looks, can get info about them with a touch, and can drop their compsure by half their wyrd with a touch.<br /> <br /> At medium to high levels of wyrd or with that new Kith merit, the Dearheart can destroy any meaningful resistance to a seduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:53:36-08:00","id":833025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833014#post833014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the Dual Kith Merit and mixed a Darkling Dearheart/Flamesiren for a demonic Succubus. He/She can see in darkness, has the sympathetic merit (what ever that is), can give someone the swoon condition, is fiery to that person's touch, gets \u2022\u2022 Striking looks, can get info about them with a touch, and can drop their compsure by half their wyrd with a touch.<br /> <br /> At medium to high levels of wyrd or with that new Kith merit, the Dearheart can destroy any meaningful resistance to a seduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stealing this as character concept, right now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:55:34-08:00","id":833026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833010#post833010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Killing Blow is weak at all. If somebody's got the Bleeding Tilts for example and you Surprise them, they're in for trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>When does Bleeding Tilt rob you of Defense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:58:34-08:00","id":833030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833026#post833026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When does Bleeding Tilt rob you of Defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surprise robs them of their defense. The Bleeding Tilt inflicts a Wound Penalty. Those two things together are required for the Corpsegrinder to get a killing blow against a living being. They only need to rob you of your Defense if you're undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:37:58-08:00","id":833049,"title":"","content":"Thosenare great! Thank you Dave!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:42:15-08:00","id":833050,"title":"","content":"Finally... Soldiers are worth playing... and actually scary as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:52:21-08:00","id":833054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833025#post833025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stealing this as character concept, right now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah imagine the character with Wyrd 9 giving the target of the seduction the Swooned Condition, then touching the target, and then forcing that persons doors. If the Target has composure \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or less, that resistance is wiped out, resistance trait based doors. The Succubus gets +2 dice from striking looks, +2 dice for the Swooned Condition, + whatever attributes/skills are being used in the seduction.<br /> <br /> One thought is a Dual Kith Illes and a Flamesiren do not mix. Flamesiren grants Striking looks merit and Illes ban the Striking Looks merit. Conflict.<br /> <br /> Soldier is all kinds of awesome. if the Soldier spends all 10 merits on fighting styles, he can literally shift and his merits daily to fit his combat needs. One day perhaps he needs a dream combat fighting style, the next kung fu, the day after that he needs to be a sniper, the day after hedge duel fighting style, the day after that a sword fighting style is best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:55:52-08:00","id":833056,"title":"","content":"I also love the flavour of a Fairest Shadowsoul, you end up looking like a character out of the Sin City movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T01:38:29-08:00","id":833117,"title":"","content":"Deleted. Didn't read something right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T03:18:11-08:00","id":833138,"title":"","content":"I liked this, especially the Wizened sections. They felt more how I'd imagine the Wizened than the previous Kith drafts.<br /> <br /> I'm still hoping for that Damsel In Distress kith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:03:02-08:00","id":833163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833138#post833138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked this, especially the Wizened sections. They felt more how I'd imagine the Wizened than the previous Kith drafts.<br /> <br /> I'm still hoping for that Damsel In Distress kith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> *bites back smart ass joke to avoid derailing thread, starts to shake, fighting to hold it in*<br /> <br /> I noticed that the dearheart kith wizen resemble the old romantic kith the way darkling dearhearts resemble succubus/incubus kith.<br /> <br /> If those dearheart wizen had observed past tendences, then the dearheart wizen would be made up of dildos, vibrators, fleshlights, anal beads, whips, and valentine's day cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-19-2016, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:29:10-08:00","id":833179,"title":"","content":"Every Flamesiren Dearheart Fairest: <a href=\"http://picolo-kun.deviantart.com/art/Is-this-safe-577105519\" target=\"_blank\">First we were like</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, <a href=\"http://picolo-kun.deviantart.com/art/Two-sides-of-a-hug-571516034\" target=\"_blank\">but then he...</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <a href=\"http://www.deviantart.com/art/5-Stages-of-Grief-585617858\" target=\"_blank\">Then we weren't.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a>==&gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I wanted to use these somewhere for <i>so long</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">P.S.: Stage 5 doesn't seem much like &quot;acceptance&quot; to me...</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:31:02-08:00","id":833181,"title":"","content":"Okay. The more 2E Changeling fluff and mechanics I see churned out, the more excited I am for when everything gets out. So on top of wanting to see more stuff on the Contracts, as well as more discussion about this &quot;Embracing the Wyrd&quot; mechanic you mentioned in passing, I'm also interested in seeing how Needle and Thread (the Virtue and Vice analogue for the Lost, I assume) will be handled.<br /> <br /> Moving on to the kiths...<br /> <br /> <b>Cleareyes </b>are definitely my favorite of this batch. I knew they were going to get Trained Observer for free, but the way their trademark senses were handled made it so much better than what I did for my stopgap conversion of the kith. Also, when I read that they weren't affected by <i>any</i> penalties due to impeded perception, does that mean Conditions/Tilts from blindness and deafness don't have as much bite for them as they do for everyone else? Either way, they're very potent spotters when you add in the benefits of (the current draft of) Clarity.<br /> <br /> The <b>Corpsegrinders</b> can make very effective assassins with their blessings, seeing as they have a good chance of killing someone (again, in the case of undead) with one blow. I do agree, though, that maybe they should also benefit from a form of regeneration. Like, maybe, the first [Wyrd] points of damage they inflict in a turn allow them to heal the same amount of bashing/lethal damage? Maybe you can limit it to every instance of a killing blow, if it's too powerful and/or overlaps with the Gristlegrinders and Leechfingers.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadowsouls</b> are also much more interesting in 2E, seeing as they can extend the bonuses of their blessing to anyone they're touching. Add in their ability to shadow walk, and you have a kith that works well for those who are assassins, scouts, and spies in terms of Attributes, Skills, and Specialties.<br /> <br /> One word on <b>Soldiers</b>. Awesome. I was instantly reminded of Taskmaster (and, to a lesser extent, Mokujin and Velvet Scarlatina). And I had this image in my head of a Soldier catching a vampire off-guard when he suddenly begins using the techniques for Kindred Duelists. All in all, another solid conversion of an offense-oriented kith to make them even <i>more</i> dangerous on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> <b>Swimmerskins</b> were handled well, with their conversion. No overlap with the other aquatic-based kiths aside from their common advantage. But seeing as their write-up was made with the assumption that a Swimmerskin has a persistent Leg Wrack, does that mean they can still swim fine even <i>if</i> they get the Tilt? I'm a bit confused there, so maybe a little clarification is in order.<br /> <br /> Like with the Soldiers, <b>Miners</b> are a lot more potent as a kith, now. I kinda was hoping they'd retain their ability to communicate via the 'morse code' of their original blessing, though. Can we expect that to make a reappearance as a Contract?<br /> <br /> For the <b>Flamesirens</b>, maybe their blessing could use a small revision to really reflect how they're &quot;too hot to handle&quot;. I don't know. Letting them have their Extreme Environment Tilt be limited to anyone with the Swooning Condition seems a bit restrictive to me. Though I can kind of understand how it could be abused. For an alternative take, though, why not let the Flamesiren be treated as an Extreme Environment of [Wyrd/2] potency, by default? And then apply the full Wyrd rating for those with the Condition? The changeling could even suppress the effect, at will.<br /> <br /> <b>Lurkgliders</b> and <b>Windwings</b> were a surprise addition, seeing as I had assumed they were folded into the Airtouched. But I'm liking them all the same, especially the Windwings. Now, they can really fly (however briefly they can manage it in each attempt).<br /> <br /> <b>Dearhearts</b> are definitely a good kith for designing nuanced characters, whether it be the manipulative Incubi and Succubi or the more genuinely sympathetic guardian angel who'll happily listen to your problems before setting off to ease your burden... one way or another. Of course, with the modular rules for making custom kiths, it should be easy to design kiths that evoke the seduction theme more strongly.<br /> <br /> <b>Steepscramblers</b> reminded me of a number of characters the same way the Solders did. In this case, it was Spiderman, Daredevil, and the Assassins from Assassin's Creed,<br /> <br /> Definitely wasn't expecting the <b>Weisse Frau</b> to become telekinetics. But I'm certainly not arguing about it, either.<br /> <br /> All in all, great work on this batch.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>PS: </b>Is Dual Kith still a thing in 2E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:32:34-08:00","id":833182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833163#post833163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those dearheart wizen had observed past tendences, then the dearheart wizen would be made up of dildos, vibrators, fleshlights, anal beads, whips, and valentine's day cards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess secret diaries; but the new style Wizened works far better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:42:20-08:00","id":833187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833181#post833181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>PS: </b>Is Dual Kith still a thing in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a Merit from Playtests files...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dual Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></span><br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not<br /> change.<br /> <br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> <br /> This Merit may only be taken once.</i><br /> <br /> My Incubus Darkling Dearheart/Flamesiren is a brain child of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Once again, thanks </span><b>Omegaphallic</b> for idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:56:29-08:00","id":833195,"title":"","content":"Here's a random thought. A Windwing buys a mundane jetpack or hang glider. Do they gain any bonuses? Does their weight count as a small child while doing so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:01:23-08:00","id":833196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833187#post833187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's a Merit from Playtests files...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dual Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></span><br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not<br /> change.<br /> <br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> <br /> This Merit may only be taken once.</i><br /> <br /> My Incubus Darkling Dearheart/Flamesiren is a brain child of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Once again, thanks </span><b>Omegaphallic</b> for idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh damn.<br /> <br /> Well, this just inspired a lot of things on the spot.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:29:29-08:00","id":833298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833187#post833187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's a Merit from Playtests files...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Dual Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022 </b></span><br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not<br /> change.<br /> <br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> <br /> This Merit may only be taken once.</i><br /> <br /> My Incubus Darkling Dearheart/Flamesiren is a brain child of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Once again, thanks </span><b>Omegaphallic</b> for idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div> Your welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah the Succubus Kith seemed like it got split in two, the Dearheart (formerly called the romantic) inheriented half including the Succubus name/discription, connection to vice and the advantage that brings.<br /> <br /> The other half of the Succubus kith seems to have gone to the Flame Siren, including striking looks \u2022\u2022 and seductive vibe.<br /> <br /> So when you use the dual kith merit to combine the red hot sex vibe (literally) of the flamesiren with the manipulative tempatations, vice knowing, and composure breaking nature of the the Dearheart and add in the Darkling's dark overtones you have not only reunited the old Succubus Kith, but made its original themes stronger.<br /> <br /> Red hot demonic seductress (or seducer), dangerous to the touch, mistress/master of fire, sex, and darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-19-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:47:28-08:00","id":833312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833298#post833298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your welcome<br /> <br /> Yeah the Succubus Kith seemed like it got split in two, the Dearheart (formerly called the romantic) inheriented half including the Succubus name/discription, connection to vice and the advantage that brings.<br /> <br /> The other half of the Succubus kith seems to have gone to the Flame Siren, including striking looks \u2022\u2022 and seductive vibe.<br /> <br /> So when you use the dual kith merit to combine the red hot sex vibe (literally) of the flamesiren with the manipulative tempatations, vice knowing, and composure breaking nature of the the Dearheart and add in the Darkling's dark overtones you have not only reunited the old Succubus Kith, but made its original themes stronger.<br /> <br /> Red hot demonic seductress (or seducer), dangerous to the touch, mistress/master of fire, sex, and darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, although on an unrelated note I also have to agree with people who think that the extreme-environment-on-touch effect shuld be affecting everyone.<br /> <br /> Regardless, as I wrote earlier:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Flamesiren Dearheart Fairest: <a href=\"http://picolo-kun.deviantart.com/art/Is-this-safe-577105519\" target=\"_blank\">First we were like</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, <a href=\"http://picolo-kun.deviantart.com/art/Two-sides-of-a-hug-571516034\" target=\"_blank\">but then he...</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <a href=\"http://picolo-kun.deviantart.com/art/5-Stages-of-Grief-585617858\" target=\"_blank\">Then we weren't.</a><a href=\"http://www.deviantart.com/art/5-Stages-of-Grief-585617858\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a>==&gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Seducers or not, they would probably be living quite the heartbroken lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:59:52-08:00","id":833325,"title":"","content":"Kiiiiinda wish the Flamesiren's mechanical bonuses didn't come with a fire-flavour. That said, since custom-kithing is explicitly allowed/encouraged in the text, it might be interesting to replace the Environment Tilt with something else (perhaps a Persistent Condition, like Addicted, Obsessed or Madness?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:33:35-08:00","id":833374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833312#post833312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, although on an unrelated note I also have to agree with people who think that the extreme-environment-on-touch effect shuld be affecting everyone.<br /> <br /> Regardless, as I wrote earlier:<br /> <br /> Seducers or not, they would probably be living quite the heartbroken lives.</div> </div> </div> </div> assuming that they're refering to an effect like extreme heat/cold as described in the Chronicles of Darkness core book, it would take hours for the flamesirens heat to kill you.<br /> <br /> His/her heat blocks or reduces the her targets ability to heal, reduces all die rolls by -1 per hour, and only becomes lethal in the sixth hour.<br /> <br /> A human with 7 health would take 12 hours of contact with the flamesiren to die, just about anything would be a quicker way to kill someone.<br /> <br /> In practice the Flamesiren would say start having sex with her target, who after a two of hours of that with will have -2 to dice pools, which the Flamesiren can use to further manipulate her target.<br /> <br /> A brief hug will in practice do nothing major to the swooned individual, they'll feel the body heat, but will be unharmed.<br /> <br /> Of course if this extreme enviroment is a different phenomenon, and it might be then all bets are off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:48:19-08:00","id":833422,"title":"","content":"So... something I missed in my excitement about the Soldiers....<br /> <br /> Does it just work for mundane Fighting Styles? It seems kind of weird that you could pick up an Uratha style that has things like going into Rage as a drawback for a maneuver if you can't enter Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:25:04-08:00","id":833443,"title":"","content":"I made a mistake they weren't refering to the extreme heat tilt, they were refering to the extreme enviroment mechanic on page 97 of thr chronicles of darkness. At low wyrd its not a big deal, but at 6 wyrd sex with a flamesiren for an hour would scar you, and at wyrd 8, you'd burn to death in a matter of turns.<br /> <br /> So Flamesiren is out, unless you wish you be lethal.<br /> <br /> Illes could do the job, perhaps better then the flamesiren, but only gets the benifit at night or in sunlight free areas.<br /> <br /> I looked up the sympathic merit that the Dearheart gets for free. For the purposes of seduction its better then Striking Looks, you accept swooned or leveraged, and you close off 2 doors automatically, along with the innate composure damping touch, you don't really need Flamesiren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:30:13-08:00","id":833444,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Fairest Thusser/Dearheart with Enchanting Performance I designed for the playtest is mechanically pretty good at seduction and distraction, particularly on crowds. The only Flamesiren benefit I'd like would be the equivalent of Striking Looks 4, but that's just a tiny quibble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:33:34-08:00","id":833488,"title":"","content":"So how do you guys think 5 dots in Potent Kith would affect a Weisse Frau's telekenesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:51:25-08:00","id":833501,"title":"","content":"The Flamesiren only gets \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 striking looks if she purcases the \u2022\u2022 striking looks merit on top of the kith blessing, the Illes on the other hand gets the basic effect of \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 striking looks (but without the actual merit) and an exceptional success on rolls that benifit from those looks, bit with the caveat that not in sunlight.<br /> <br /> Another cool Dearheart mix would be to make an Apsara by combing Dearheart and Nix, with the Elemental Seeming. I'd take the contract that allows you to pull objects, and if your an elemental a person, from a reflection, pull a copy of yourself out.<br /> <br /> For a Darkling Dearheart to gain more of a magical seduction feel all you really need is Vainglory \u2022\u2022\u2022, when can cause the swooned condition when using envoys splendor, and Beautiful Madness if buffed by Darklings. Its resisted by Composure which the Dearheart can dampen.<br /> <br /> I have two questions about Vainglory, if a character gets vainglory at \u2022\u2022\u2022, getting two of the effects, can the changeling use both on a single activation? How about two seperate uses of the contract, like one turn you use Envoy and the next Madness, and have them working at the same time?<br /> <br /> If you can get the benifit of both on asingle use of the contract, then you could get the darkling +3 benifit on the activation roll for both.<br /> <br /> Either way you could give those around you both the swooning and delusional condition.<br /> <br /> I also wonder what happens when you scour your mask while using Vainglory, can you still do that without disurping Vainglory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-19-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:09:11-08:00","id":833550,"title":"","content":"Are mask and mein now needle and thread on the sheet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:05:40-08:00","id":833619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833550#post833550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are mask and mein now needle and thread on the sheet?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are referred to as Virtue/Vice, Masque/Mein and Needle/Thread depending on which part of the documents you look at, presumably because they're all at various stages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T20:54:12-08:00","id":833690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was just wondering what the official decision was because I'm building a sheet for my players for tomorrow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:32:58-08:00","id":833932,"title":"","content":"Not being familiar with the Weisse Frau from 1E or the specific myths, the kith description seems really disconnected from the kith abilities, to the point I just assumed it was a typo at first. Maybe tweak something there to hint at the telekinesis in the description, or give them an ability more linked to the empathy the kith descriptions talks about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:43:22-08:00","id":833942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833932#post833932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being familiar with the Weisse Frau from 1E or the specific myths, the kith description seems really disconnected from the kith abilities, to the point I just assumed it was a typo at first. Maybe tweak something there to hint at the telekinesis in the description, or give them an ability more linked to the empathy the kith descriptions talks about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have the same feeling. I'm not an expert in german folklore, but it seems to me that the Kiss of Life power of the first edition capture the feeling of the kith better than this telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T15:30:46-08:00","id":834088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=833501#post833501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Flamesiren only gets \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 striking looks if she purcases the \u2022\u2022 striking looks merit on top of the kith blessing, the Illes on the other hand gets the basic effect of \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 striking looks (but without the actual merit) and an exceptional success on rolls that benifit from those looks, bit with the caveat that not in sunlight.<br /> <br /> Another cool Dearheart mix would be to make an Apsara by combing Dearheart and Nix, with the Elemental Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could create a Flamesiren/Illes/Dearheart if you take the Pilgrims of the Endless Road Entitlement. That would be one hell of a combo.<br /> <br /> Now that I'm thinking about it, Flamesiren/Illes would basically be Yvaine from Neil Gaiman's Stardust.<br /> <br /> <i>That</i> makes me wonder, what Kiths would other modern fairytale characters be. Like in Once Upon a Time Henry or Regina. I have no idea about Henry, Regina may be a reformed Darkling remade into Fairest, or maybe a Fae Actor turned changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T16:03:29-08:00","id":834098,"title":"","content":"Henry would be Author.<br /> <br /> Regina Witchtooth/Flamesiren Darkling, any dude that gets close to her gets burned (metaphorucally).<br /> <br /> Emma Riddle Kith Fairest.<br /> <br /> Red, Hunterheart Beast.<br /> <br /> Dwarves, Wizened Miners.<br /> <br /> Jimmy Cricket, Dearheart Beast, with zero merits in striking looks.<br /> <br /> Hook is hard, Darkling Soldier.<br /> <br /> Charming Fairest Soldier.<br /> <br /> Many of the less magical characters, like Mulan Soldiers with varying Seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T16:09:18-08:00","id":834102,"title":"","content":"Sarah Walker from Chuck, Larcenist/Deartheart or Whisperwisp Darkling with the striking looks merit. She fits Darkling Fluff wise, but blessing wise fits Fairest better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:02:29-08:00","id":836797,"title":"","content":"Hey, something just struck me. <br /> <br /> Do Miners need to sleep? They suffer no penalties from exhaustion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:16:16-08:00","id":836807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=836797#post836797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, something just struck me.<br /> <br /> Do Miners need to sleep? They suffer no penalties from exhaustion</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadbacks also don't suffer exhaustion penalties.<br /> <br /> I tend to err on the side that if it doesn't explicitly state you no longer need to X, then you still have to. What Broadbacks and Miners can do is simply have the same dice pool no matter how many days they've gone without sleep, or how much physical effort they've made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T21:37:53-08:00","id":837385,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to why are there no kiths focused on dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T23:23:09-08:00","id":837404,"title":"","content":"Because every changeling is focused on dreams? That and the True Fae wouldn't need that sort of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T02:13:13-08:00","id":837446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837404#post837404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because every changeling is focused on dreams? That and the True Fae wouldn't need that sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, every changeling is also focused on escaping, and there are kiths that make some better at it than others.<br /> <br /> secondly, I think you're confusing kiths and the abilities derived from kiths. Gentry don't make mannequin's just because they want the changeling to be more resilient toward resisting exhaustion; that's just a byproduct of the kith they were changed to. So easily there could be a changeling that was made for a purpose that also allows them a higher degree of manipulation in dreams, or extra dice in dream related rolls.<br /> <br /> True fae are weird beings, and to say the true fae wouldn't need something is pretty meta, as I'm sure the true fae could need anything if it solidified their story, <br /> <br /> but back to the point,from a design point of view. Are there going to be any kiths that feature dream related abilities, and if not, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T09:51:22-08:00","id":837631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837446#post837446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, every changeling is also focused on escaping, and there are kiths that make some better at it than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hollow comparison - &quot;escaping&quot; is not a category as broad as &quot;basically the laws of physics&quot; in Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:37:56-08:00","id":837656,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can put this a simpler way.<br /> <br /> Dreams are stories. Fae are stories. Every Fae, therefore, is a dream.* It's harder to justify specializing stuff like that. It's like specializing in breathing(Maybe not a great comparison, but still)<br /> <br /> *This, by the way,was the logic that led to changelings physically entering dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T12:54:43-08:00","id":837720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837656#post837656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me see if I can put this a simpler way.<br /> <br /> Dreams are stories. Fae are stories. Every Fae, therefore, is a dream.* It's harder to justify specializing stuff like that. It's like specializing in breathing(Maybe not a great comparison, but still)<br /> <br /> *This, by the way,was the logic that led to changelings physically entering dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but..but there are kiths that specialize in breathing....underwater!<br /> I'm just jabbing, thank you for your response","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:19:53-08:00","id":837735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837656#post837656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me see if I can put this a simpler way.<br /> <br /> Dreams are stories. Fae are stories. Every Fae, therefore, is a dream.* It's harder to justify specializing stuff like that. It's like specializing in breathing(Maybe not a great comparison, but still)<br /> <br /> *This, by the way,was the logic that led to changelings physically entering dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a logical fallacy.<br /> <br /> That's like saying cats are mammals. Dogs are mammals. There for Dogs are Cats.<br /> <br /> Still I get what you saying, its an inheriant part of Changeling nature, so a Kith specializing in dreams is redundant. It makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:28:50-08:00","id":837741,"title":"","content":"Because the Fae care about logical fallacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:19:42-08:00","id":837768,"title":"","content":"LMFAO good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:43:10-08:00","id":837777,"title":"","content":"Plus, IIRC David said something about merits related to subsystems (including dreams) not being released yet. So even if there arent any Kiths focused on dreams, there are still changelings who've adapted to oneiromancy more so than others. It makes sense, and leaves your kith open for other flavoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:51:36-08:00","id":837856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837777#post837777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, IIRC David said something about merits related to subsystems (including dreams) not being released yet. So even if there arent any Kiths focused on dreams, there are still changelings who've adapted to oneiromancy more so than others. It makes sense, and leaves your kith open for other flavoring.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool, so there could be more merits related to dreams, pledges, and other subsystems.<br /> <br /> What other Changeling subsystems might have merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T20:12:18-08:00","id":837892,"title":"","content":"What happens when a Dearheart touch or touch plus sympathy merit produces a social manvuever with zero doors?<br /> <br /> Like the Dearheart drops someones composure to zero, eliminating all their basic doors and uses sympathetic to eliminate any doors for things like going against the targets virtue?<br /> <br /> What happens when you goal has no doirs thanks to supernatural means, do you automatically succeed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:00:58-08:00","id":837910,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. The alternative would be... you still have to roll once which you'll probably make easily?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T02:47:51-08:00","id":837988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837892#post837892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a Dearheart touch or touch plus sympathy merit produces a social manvuever with zero doors?<br /> <br /> Like the Dearheart drops someones composure to zero, eliminating all their basic doors and uses sympathetic to eliminate any doors for things like going against the targets virtue?<br /> <br /> What happens when you goal has no doirs thanks to supernatural means, do you automatically succeed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doors are still capped at 1 at minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T05:49:07-08:00","id":838007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837988#post837988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doors are still capped at 1 at minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T13:07:09-08:00","id":838187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=837446#post837446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> but back to the point,from a design point of view. Are there going to be any kiths that feature dream related abilities, and if not, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this obviously isn't an official kith, but here's a rough stab at one I made if you're interested:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamstalker</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">She was just standing there when I woke up. She leaned down, kissed me on the forehead, and whispered &quot;I told you I knew where you slept.&quot; Then she was gone. I swear, I'm never sleeping again.</span><br /> <br /> Dreamstalkers are unusual for changelings, as most of them spent little time in their Keepers' lands. A dreamstalker is invariable tasked with haunting mortal dreamscapes, collecting information or bestowing blessings and curses on the Gentry's behalf. Some are used to delight mortals, plying them with dreams of wonders just out of reach, calling them slowly but surely into their Keepers' arms. Others visit nightmares upon those who have commit some transgression against the Gentry, making each night another battle for the mortal's sanity. While an escaping dreamstalker may think freedom to be only a mortal dream away, she finds that no matter how far she runs, every night pulls her dangerously close to where she started.<br /> <br /> -<b>Beast:</b> They are made up of creatures omnipresent in a nightmare, such as a humanoid figure composed of countless crawling spiders or a tangled mass of branch and wire filled with staring red-eyed crows.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Constantly shifting features and colors, never the same twice, yet somehow always recognizable as the same entity.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> Beautiful dream lovers, too perfect to be human, beckoning seductively.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Little imps with constantly twitching fingers and glowing symbols forming from the multi-colored sands pouring from cracks in their skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Dreamstalkers gain the Dreamsteps Contract for free, and gain an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5 when rolling for the Contract's activation. Additionally, a dreamstalker may spend a point of Glamour when touching a mortal to mark them. A dreamstalker instantly knows whenever a marked mortal has fallen asleep, and by spending another point of Glamour, this mortal is treated as though they were nearby for the purposes of the Dreamsteps Contract, allowing the dreamstalker to travel through their dreams from a distance. A dreamstalker may only have a number of mortals equal to their Wyrd marked in this manner, although they can erase a mark at any time by spending another point of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T15:16:04-08:00","id":838246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=838187#post838187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this obviously isn't an official kith, but here's a rough stab at one I made if you're interested:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamstalker</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">She was just standing there when I woke up. She leaned down, kissed me on the forehead, and whispered &quot;I told you I knew where you slept.&quot; Then she was gone. I swear, I'm never sleeping again.</span><br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:22:27-08:00","id":838329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832889-moar-kiths?p=838187#post838187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this obviously isn't an official kith, but here's a rough stab at one I made if you're interested:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamstalker</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">She was just standing there when I woke up. She leaned down, kissed me on the forehead, and whispered &amp;quot;I told you I knew where you slept.&amp;quot; Then she was gone. I swear, I'm never sleeping again.</span><br /> <br /> Dreamstalkers are unusual for changelings, as most of them spent little time in their Keepers' lands. A dreamstalker is invariable tasked with haunting mortal dreamscapes, collecting information or bestowing blessings and curses on the Gentry's behalf. Some are used to delight mortals, plying them with dreams of wonders just out of reach, calling them slowly but surely into their Keepers' arms. Others visit nightmares upon those who have commit some transgression against the Gentry, making each night another battle for the mortal's sanity. While an escaping dreamstalker may think freedom to be only a mortal dream away, she finds that no matter how far she runs, every night pulls her dangerously close to where she started.<br /> <br /> -<b>Beast:</b> They are made up of creatures omnipresent in a nightmare, such as a humanoid figure composed of countless crawling spiders or a tangled mass of branch and wire filled with staring red-eyed crows.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> Constantly shifting features and colors, never the same twice, yet somehow always recognizable as the same entity.<br /> <b>-Fairest:</b> Beautiful dream lovers, too perfect to be human, beckoning seductively.<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> Little imps with constantly twitching fingers and glowing symbols forming from the multi-colored sands pouring from cracks in their skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Dreamstalkers gain the Dreamsteps Contract for free, and gain an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5 when rolling for the Contract's activation. Additionally, a dreamstalker may spend a point of Glamour when touching a mortal to mark them. A dreamstalker instantly knows whenever a marked mortal has fallen asleep, and by spending another point of Glamour, this mortal is treated as though they were nearby for the purposes of the Dreamsteps Contract, allowing the dreamstalker to travel through their dreams from a distance. A dreamstalker may only have a number of mortals equal to their Wyrd marked in this manner, although they can erase a mark at any time by spending another point of Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's neat, which just a touch of the disurbing and chilling well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T08:49:33-08:00","id":839940,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for the compliments. I'm glad that you liked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:04:56-08:00","id":839994,"title":"","content":"You welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:28:09-08:00","id":840054,"title":"","content":"I was messing with some kiths, trying to create new ones, and here one of my favorites:<br /> (PS: I'm not very good at describing seemings, or quotes, or durances... damn.)<br /> <br /> <b>Maze Architect (Troll modified)</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Hey, Steve, it's almost midnight, don't you think its about time to make a place to sleep?</span></i><br /> <br /> The human architeture always have enchanted the Fae, but the secret passages, tunnels and crazy houses is one of the most iconic features in the fantastic architeture. Some Gentry like to gather humans to design and construct ellegant houses with complex systems of vaults, tunnels and secret entries.<br /> <br /> <b>-Darkling: </b>A strange entity who seems to be covered entirely with bitumen.<br /> <b>-Elemental:</b> A strange humanoid amount of bricks who can move and merge with the walls.<br /> <b>-Beast:</b> A half-man half-ox monster, holding a gigantic axe. <i>(Thanks Omegaphallic</i>)<br /> <b>-Wizened:</b> A worker with a safety helment and mechanical arms attached to his body who can lift good amounts of cement.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The architect gain the Unseen Senses(Secret Passages) merit for free. Spend a point of Glamour and mark the perimeter of an area to create a temporary Safe Place Merit. The level of the Merit is equal to half the changeling\u2019s Wyrd (round up) and the effect lasts for 24 hours from creation or until she leaves, whichever is longer. The area can manifest secret passages and/or tunnels that increase the difficulty for finding the Architet as per Safe Place. Sometimes, a new tunnel or secret passage is created without the knowledge of the architet.<br /> <br /> The effect manifest underground and above ground in different ways:<br /> Above ground: You need the materials to construct the Safe Place(cement, bricks, etc). Or you can modify houses that haven't had any owners for at least a year and a day.<br /> Underground: You can create tunnels with rocks and earth, but you still need materials for doors, locks, etc.<br /> <br /> You can turn the effect of the merit permanent with Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 03-01-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:24:21-0